WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.967
Explore stations with their own covers and switch between music and voices. Sample stations and playback are simulated.

2
00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:10.267
Browse different station identities: City Pulse, Nightfall Jazz and Morning Stories.

3
00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:16.833
The repeater panel shows listeners and upload. These changing traffic figures are simulated for the demonstration.

4
00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:20.000
Now the real studio: give your station a name, description and cover.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.967
Choose Phone to broadcast directly over Tor. Relay and Icecast destinations are also available.

6
00:00:23.967 --> 00:00:30.967
Keep public listing off for this recording, then start the real Tor broadcast. Connection waits are shortened.

7
00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:36.300
Load two local audio files. The first plays on air while the second waits in the queue.

8
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.633
Adjust the music level and trigger a crossfade to the next track.

9
00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:48.933
Watch the real music and on-air meters. The microphone stays off in this music-only recording.

10
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:54.533
Trigger an original station ID from a pad. Each pad can hold a different audio clip.

11
00:00:54.533 --> 00:00:59.533
Set voice ducking, crossfade duration and silence skipping from the studio controls.
